index 85a03364..121e18d8 100644
--- a/docs/reference/config.rst
+++ b/docs/reference/config.rst
@@ -2349,6 +2349,27 @@ separators:
 Multiple dots can be escaped in the same key: ``-x 'some\.dotted\.name.key=val'``. A backslash not followed by a dot
 passes through literally.
 
+Substitutions inside an override
+================================
+
+.. versionadded:: 4.61
+
+An override value goes through the same substitution pass as a value written in the configuration file, so
+``{posargs}``, ``{posargs:default}``, ``{env:VAR}`` and ``{env_name}`` are resolved instead of being passed to the
+environment as literal text:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   tox -x env_run_base.commands='pytest {posargs:tests}' -e py -- -k slow
+
+This runs ``pytest -k slow`` (the ``-- -k slow`` is consumed as the positional arguments, so the ``tests`` default of
+``{posargs:tests}`` is not used, and the environment itself never sees ``{posargs:tests}``).
+
+.. note::
+
+   Overrides always use the ini spelling of a substitution, even in a TOML project, because they are parsed with the
+   ini string rules.
+
 ***********
  TOML only
 ***********
